      "claim": "Hesperidin, a glycosylated polyphenol with the highest transfer score, was detected in mouse brain after oral administration and distributed to brain tissues, directly demonstrating that glycoside-containing polyphenols can achieve meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "A phenylethanoid glycoside was detected in rat hippocampus and striatum after oral administration, providing independent in vivo evidence that neutral glycosides can cross the blood-brain barrier.",
